nt.com/u/134593944?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xcpn","html_url":"https://github.com/xcpn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xcpn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xcpn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xcpn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xcpn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xcpn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xcpn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xcpn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xcpn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xcpn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-19T16:22:16Z","updated_at":"2025-07-20T11:53:21Z","body":"I also don't understand this change, this messed up some other stuff on my server.\n\nI have two services on my Debian server, `headscale.example.com` and `ntfy.example.com`.\n\nIf I change `base_domain` to `example.com` and have `tailscale set --accept-dns=true` (the Debian server is also a node configured as exit-node), I can't even send notifications via NTFY from the server.\n\nI now need to disable `--accept-dns` and re-enable every time I want to send a notification using curl, otherwise I get `curl: (6) Could not resolve host: ntfy.example.com`.\n\nCan you comment on that @kradalby, what's the reason we can't use the same url? Maybe I could change the `base_domain` to `headscale2.example.com` even though that subdomain doesn't exist?\n\nEdit: Actually, this change is better. Don't know if this is the reason they removed the option to have both `server_url` and `base_domain` the same, but it actually introduced a problem by having both of them set to `headscale.example.com`.\n\nIf I have `server_url` and `base_domain` the same, and also have configured the Tailscale client with `tailscale set --accept-dns=true`, then something weird is happening with commands such as the one below. Assuming has to do with the fact that MagicDNS is same as the Headscale domain and everything is being used on the same system?\n\n```\n~# openssl s_client -servername headscale.example.com -connect headscale.example.com:443 | openssl x509 -noout -dates\n```\n\nThis throws errors and doesn't return the dates for the certificate. This is why it introduced issued with my `ntfy.example.com` service too when I changed the `base_domain` to just `example.com`. I now changed it to `magic.example.com` and everything is fine.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/3092437472/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"xcpn","id":134593944,"node_id":"U_kgDOCAW9mA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/134593944?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xcpn","html_url":"https://github.com/xcpn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xcpn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xcpn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xcpn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xcpn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xcpn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xcpn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xcpn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xcpn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xcpn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":18712040987,"node_id":"MEE_lADOEFLz886zo8XqzwAAAARbUxYb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/events/18712040987","actor":{"login":"kradalby","id":98431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NDMx","avatar_ur